id: pm-gh1605
title: "GH-1605: Preserve recent events when default history output must be bounded"
description: "**Version:** pm 2026.10.26, non-git tracker, one item with 251 history entries (two concurrent writers, 50 ops each).\n\n**Repro**\n```sh\npm history <id>              # default\npm history <id> --limit 5    # \"Latest n entries\"\n```\n**Observed:** the default read renders entries **1–183** oldest-first, hits the output ceiling and returns `has_more: true, truncated: true`; the **68 newest entries — including the latest handoff/update — are not in the answer**. It costs 15,960 bytes. `--limit 5` returns entries 247–251 in 815 bytes.\n\n**Expected:** when the default history read must truncate, it should keep the newest entries (and point to the cursor for older ones), or default to a bounded recent window with an explicit way to page back to the start. History verification itself is fine (all 251 entries verify); this is only about which end of the timeline survives truncation.\n\n**Why it matters for agents:** \"what happened last on this item?\" is the normal handoff question. With the current default an agent spends ~16 KB of context on the oldest events and still needs a second call to see the current state — about 95% of the bytes are avoidable for that question.\n\n\nIntake boundary: this is a report against published 2026.10.26, not proof of a current-checkout defect. Reproduce in an external sandbox before implementation. Related completed work retains its shipped scope. Proposed examples or categories are not accepted contracts until validated.\n\nSource: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1605"
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags[3]: agent-ux,github,sdk
created_at: "2026-10-26T19:02:04.414Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-26T19:02:04.414Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: "Reproduce the reported 251-entry timeline in an external non-Git tracker and measure the selected entries and rendered bytes.; A bounded default keeps the most recent events with correct original numbering, complete counts and executable older-page recovery; explicit full reads preserve complete chronological history.; SDK, CLI and MCP selection and continuation semantics remain consistent, with no duplicate or skipped entries and no change to integrity verification."
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: medium
confidence: medium
expected_result: "The ordinary recent-history question retains the latest handoff within its budget and offers explicit, lossless continuation to older entries."
